// Cursor's Electron runtime arguments (JSON with comments — the app's own
// "Preferences: Configure Runtime Arguments" edits this same file).
//
// Chromium picks its credential backend from XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, and
// "Hyprland" is not one of the desktops it recognises, so it silently falls
// back to the plaintext `basic` store and reports "An OS keyring couldn't be
// identified for storing the encryption related data in your current desktop
// environment" on every launch. Naming the backend here points it at
// gnome-keyring over libsecret instead. Both halves are required: the package
// (shared/pacman.txt) and this line.
{
	"password-store": "gnome-libsecret"
}
